.TH QEMU-RDP 1 "2026" "wsh-qemu-rdp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qemu-rdp \- RDP server for QEMU's D-Bus display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qemu-rdp
[\fB\-\-dbus\-address\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
.B serve
[\fB\-\-bind\-address\fR \fIIP\fR:\fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-cert\fR \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\-key\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-credentials\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-codecs\fR \fISPEC\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qemu-rdp
serves the console of a QEMU started with \fB\-display dbus\fR (the bus name org.qemu) to RDP
clients: the screen (RemoteFX and bitmap codecs), keyboard and mouse, the sound of
\fB\-audiodev dbus\fR through rdpsnd (PCM or Opus, 48 kHz), resizing and a text clipboard. Clients
log in with NLA (CredSSP over TLS) with the one user name and password the server has; without
them every client is refused.
.PP
On Proxmox VE with the wsh-pve qemu-server, run it through the unit
\fBwsh-qemu-rdp@\fIvmid\fB.service\fR instead (\fBsystemctl enable \-\-now wsh-qemu-rdp@\fIvmid\fR), which
reads \fI/etc/wsh-qemu-rdp/<vmid>.conf\fR (written with a generated password at its first start) and
connects to the VM's bus, \fI/run/wsh-dbus-display/<vmid>.sock\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dbus\-address " " \fIADDRESS\fR
The D-Bus address of QEMU's display (default: the session bus).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bind\-address " " \fIIP\fR:\fIPORT\fR
The address to listen on (default 0.0.0.0:3389).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cert " " \fIFILE\fR ", " \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
The TLS certificate and private key (PEM); without them, server-cert.pem and server-key.pem in
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/qemu-rdp\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-credentials\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
The user name on the first line, the password on the second (a wsh-pve addition). They can also be
set with the D-Bus method SetCredentials of org.QemuDisplay.RDP, where the bus lets qemu-rdp own
that name.
.TP
.BR \-\-codecs " " \fISPEC\fR
IronRDP's codec configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-capabilities
Print the program's capabilities as JSON.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QEMURDP_LOG
The log filter (error, warn (default), info, debug, trace).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://gitlab.com/marcandre.lureau/qemu-display
